  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;be the maximum integral value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> for which the roots of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;are rational. Then the area of the region <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is",
    "image": null
  },
